## Agentic Workflow

Use `/implement-orchestrator` to execute plans step-by-step. The plan can come from any source — a file, conversation context, or description. Each step is implemented, reviewed via `/simplify`, and committed separately.

### Skill Entry Points

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `/implement-orchestrator` | Run the step-by-step pipeline from any plan source |
| `/plan-codebase` | Generate a code specification for a step |
| `/plan-tests` | Generate a test plan for a step |
| `/implement-parallel` | Dispatch parallel Impl Coder and Test Coder for a step |
| `/review-parallel` | Run parallel code reviews with severity-based consensus |
| `/clean-code-planner` | Apply clean code principles before any code change |
| `/simplify` | Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency |
| `/make-pr` | Create or update a PR — runs gates, fixes errors, links issues, assigns reviewers |

## Context Management

For long tasks, use `$IMPL_TMP/progress.md` to track state (`$IMPL_TMP` resolves to `~/.claude/impl-tmp/<repo>/<branch>`). Use `/clear` then continue with the progress file. Temporary artifacts are stored outside the repo and cleaned up automatically when the orchestrator finishes.

